// The case table of the switch being walked: casv[i] is the case value's
// expression node (-1 for `default`, which the parser spells as a case whose
// value is -1), casb[i] is the block that case starts.
//
// It is a stack, not a table: a switch records the length on entry as its
// mark, appends while it walks its body, builds its dispatch chain from
// [mark, len), then drops back to the mark. Nested switches therefore work
// without a second structure.

case_mark() {
  int i = len((import casv));
} return int i;
given cfg_init ():(0)
